Purpose:
Module-related requests ka actual business logic handle karta hai.

createModule()

Purpose:
Naya module create karke MongoDB mein save karta hai.

Request Data:

title
description
order
difficulty
estimatedTime

Process:

req.body se module ki information receive karta hai.
Required fields ki validation karta hai.
Module.create() ke through MongoDB mein module save karta hai.
Success par 201 response return karta hai.
Error hone par 500 response return karta hai.

Endpoint:
POST /api/modules

Success Response:
Created module aur success message return karta hai.

getModules()

Purpose:
MongoDB se saare available modules retrieve karta hai.

Process:

Module.find() se modules fetch karta hai.
sort({ order: 1 }) ke through modules ko sequence/order ke according ascending order mein arrange karta hai.
Modules ko JSON response ke through frontend/client ko return karta hai.
Error hone par 500 response return karta hai.

Endpoint:

GET /api/modules

Input:
Koi request body required nahi hai.

Output:
Saare modules ordered format mein return hote hain.